# Aikido scanner ignore rules for qaudion-ios.
#
# Rules use gitignore-style syntax. Every rule is paired with a rationale so
# a future reviewer (or an auditor asking why an Aikido finding was silenced)
# can verify the decision without re-doing the triage.
#
# Scope:
#   * True positives are fixed in code, NOT silenced here.
#   * Ignore rules are for documented false positives, third-party vendored
#     code we don't own, or structural scanner limitations.
#
# When adding a rule: paste the Aikido issue title + sub-issue ID in the
# comment so we can cross-reference with the dashboard.
#
# Status as of 2026-08-21:
#   This repo is NOT YET CONNECTED to the Aikido dashboard (no findings have
#   been triaged here). Placeholder file added to match the convention used
#   in bcrypto-server, qaudion-android-new, and qaudion-desktop, so the
#   moment this repo is connected in Aikido's external dashboard, the triage
#   file already exists in the expected location/format and the first real
#   findings can be added here following the numbered-section pattern used
#   in the sibling repos' .aikidoignore files.
#
# No rules yet — nothing to ignore because no scan has run against this
# repo's Swift/Xcode sources.
